\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Lifecycle cost vector}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{compute}

\p{The \strong{lifecycle cost} of protocol #{P} is the vector}

##{
  C(P)=(C_{\mathrm{roll}},C_{\mathrm{env}},C_{\mathrm{ver}},
        C_{\mathrm{upd}},C_{\mathrm{replay}},C_{\mathrm{ckpt}},
        C_{\mathrm{eval}}).
}

\p{The coordinates charge rollout generation, environment execution, verifier
work, proposed updates, replay bookkeeping, checkpoint or predictor work, and
evaluation. Each coordinate must declare a physical unit or a conversion to a
common accounting unit.}

\p{This vector is an FTIP proposal motivated by distinct empirical accounts.
Token-based pretraining scaling appears in \citef{kaplan2020scaling}.
Compute-optimal scaling appears in \citef{hoffmann2022training}.}

\p{Rollout reuse changes generation and update counts in
\citef{miao2026when}.}

\p{Checkpoint extrapolation adds fitting and recovery work in
\citef{chen2026lowrank}. The vector preserves these differences.}
